  "review_notes": [
    "Variant WLC.2KI.19.23.v001 resolved to r00-base, covering s010 and s011; the projection is aligned as printed (rule 9).",
    "Both marginal notes were read and set aside; the printed text governs (rule 38).",
    "Chapter reconciliation: the supplied the of תand הtall cedars thereof was moved from the rectum אֲרָזָיו to the construct קוֹמַת, so that both attributive chains in this verse divide alike and both agree with 19.21 and 19.26. Rule 29 places a construct chain's determiners and permits a supplied the on the construct where no article morpheme is present; rule 15's direction to read the noun of the expression rather than its leftmost word governs a numeral and the noun it counts.",
    "The competing reading, which the accepted alignment took for קוֹמַת, gives the the to אֲרָזָיו as the English phrase's head noun; it is set aside because the rectum carries no article morpheme and rule 29 is what counts a chain's the's."
